{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1534905-risen-and-the-world-of-darkness","id":1534905,"title":"Risen and the World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-29T09:30:56-07:00","id":1534905,"title":"Risen and the World of Darkness","content":"The title of this topic came form pag.53 of The Risen book. In that section various point of view about the Risen are quoted from different sources. Some of them quite... strange.<br /> Risen are sturdy by WtO standards and dangerous enemies due to the threat they pose on others' Fetters but... nothing comparable to anything in the skinlands. I understand that they are written for telling stories of revenge (The Crow) and not direct conflicts or antagonists for other splats, but even with Serendipity and Fascinate I cannot comprehend how canon they should pose a threat to Vampires and Lupines. Most Arcanoi are a problem in the skinlands when you have a body, they have a lot of limitations. How can be explained the fear they instill in Vampires and Lupines?<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires</b> - Joseph Ordonez, Sabbat pack priest<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know what the fuck it was, and I don't fucking care! It took a full clip in the chest and stood there, leaking green shit outta the holes, like it was a walk in the effingpark! I've been Sabbat for 10 years, I've seen all kinda shit in my day, even an effing Baali, but nothing ever put the fear of God in me like that thing. </div> </div> </div><b>Lupines</b> - Angela Dalsimer (Collects-Old-Tales), Ragabash of the Fianna\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Stay out of their way. I've seen three of these walking corpses in my time, and heard tell of a dozen others, and none had a quarrel with us unless quarreled with first. It is best to let them find their own path, and not stand in the middle of it. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26404-submariner93","name":"Submariner93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26404_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-29T22:27:21-07:00","id":1534929,"title":"","content":"Some of this may be due to a disconnect between the intended flavor text (a relentless undead in pursuit of its objective/vengenace) and the actual mechanics. However, there are some important things to remember.<br /> <br /> 1) Risen do not suffer any penalties to their dice pool unless the damage is aggravated. Vampires treat Lethal damage as Bashing, but they still take dice pool penalties. So they are used to seeing other vampires suffer in ways that Risen do not.<br /> <br /> 2) Lots of things that cause aggravated damage to other supernatural creatures do not cause aggravated damage to Risen. Fire and claw/bite attacks from supernatural creatures are pretty much it (granted both vampires and werewolves usually have access to those).<br /> <br /> 3) Risen can take a lot more damage than other creatures. Vampires and werewolves have seven health levels which impose dice pool penalties. Risen have ten Corpus levels (that might not provide any dice pool penalties when damaged) and can be healed by Pathos. Furthermore, if reduced to zero health levels, they are only unconscious for a limited amount of time. As long as the Risen still has some Pathos, they can usually regain consciousness within 24 hours. This is much quicker than vampires. Furthermore, if worse comes to worse, the Risen can always transfer control to their Shadow who then can heal the body with its Angst.<br /> <br /> So the result is often the impression that nothing can stop one of the Risen. It can take a lot more damage than any other creature and not seem to suffer any penalties for it. It's just futile to fight them. After you fire all the bullets in your gun and it doesn't seem to affect them at all, what do you? Reload and fire again (why if it did nothing the first time)? Or just run away?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, they also have access to Celerity, Fortitude, Potence, and Obfuscate (I personally choose to interpret that they have special Arcanoi that work the same as these powers rather than them using actual vampiric Disciplines). So with Fortitude they now soak aggravated and have even more health levels. Enough Celerity and Potence they are going to do decent damage. Not hard for them to defeat a vampire one on one. Armed with silver, they can deal good damage to a werewolf.<br /> <br /> A single Risen wouldn't be a threat to an entire group of vampires or werewolves. But I could see it scaring the hell out of a single vampire or werewolf.<br /> <br /> And we should remember that given their rarity, very little is known about them. All the vampire may know is that someone they killed has come back. They don't know about their limitations, the Conduit, or anything else. All they know is what they observe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T05:23:51-07:00","id":1534938,"title":"","content":"Indeed, from the quoted text I see that the vampire is a very new one (only ten years? still a baby), maybe he has some bias, knowing nothing of the world. Are Risen a recurring element in Wraith or after '96 they have been forgotten? I think I never read about them in other WtO books (my knowledge is limited, I admit, and maybe focused too much on the shadowlands).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26404-submariner93","name":"Submariner93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26404_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T14:25:12-07:00","id":1534961,"title":"","content":"There's no reason to think that as a concept the Risen have been removed as a setting element. It's just there's been no reason to revisit them since the original sourcebook. The Wraith 20th corebook has an entire chapter on them.<br /> <br /> Even though the Risen sourcebook was released as part of the Wraith setting, it might have been better to release it as part of the general World of Darkness line like Mummy, the original Sorcerer, and other &quot;universal&quot; sourcebooks. Risen characters are more likely to be used in those games taking place in the physical world than the underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T07:39:14-07:00","id":1535003,"title":"","content":"Also, Vampires taking bashing damage from bullets was introduced in Revised. Risen was written before that. When Risen was written, bullets lethal damage to both kinds of undead, but Risen had larger health pools and no wound penalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T07:49:14-07:00","id":1535005,"title":"","content":"Ah, this would nicely explain the Sabbat entry!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26404-submariner93","name":"Submariner93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26404_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}